{'type': 'doc', 'version': 1, 'content': [{'type': 'paragraph', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'For this ticket, I think it is more of a subtle “bad” user experience in the case where '}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'we should have respected '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'mon_max_pg_per_osd', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'text', 'text': '. What I think happened in the high level of scheme is that when we initally create pools with --bulk flag, we basically already at near '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'mon_max_pg_per_osd', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'text', 'text': ', especially when we land on a pg_num that quantized to the nearest power of two. We pushed it over through creating new pools that will have at least 32 pg by default without consulting the autoscaler module. Therefore, we would get a HEALTH_WARN regarding  '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'too many PGs per OSD (256 > max 250)', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'I think one thing that we could do is that we should use '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'mon_max_pg_per_osd', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'text', 'text': ' as a hard ceiling '}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'something like:'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'max_allowed = root_map[root_id].osd_count * self.mon_max_pg_per_osd', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'and then:'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'In OSDMonitor::prepare_pool_create()'}]}, {'type': 'codeBlock', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'uint64_t total_pgs = calculate_total_pgs_after_creation();
uint64_t max_allowed = num_osds * g_conf->mon_max_pg_per_osd;

if (total_pgs > max_allowed) {
    ss << "Cannot create pool: would exceed mon_max_pg_per_osd ("
       << total_pgs << " > " << max_allowed << ")";
    return -ENOSPC;
}'}]}, {'type': 'paragraph', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'with exception only when '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'ceph osd pool create new-pool --force-pg-limit', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}]}]}

{'type': 'doc', 'version': 1, 'content': [{'type': 'paragraph', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '[ Sharing my analysis --- ', 'marks': [{'type': 'strong'}]}, {'type': 'text', 'text': ' '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'Internal Do no share with customer]', 'marks': [{'type': 'strong'}]}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'hardBreak'}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'I traced the code changes for OPEN operations using strace and found that the client is requesting claim type 4, which corresponds to CLAIM_FH = 4. Inside the '}, {'type': 'text', 'text': 'open4_validate_claim()', 'marks': [{'type': 'code'}]}, {'type': 'text', 'text': ' function, I encountered the relevant code path that leads to the claim validation failure.'}], 'attrs': {'localId': '6d3714cb9c0f'}}, {'type': 'codeBlock', 'attrs': {'localId': '24d1c624-31eb-4b2d-8271-a86ed2d6efcd'}, 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '/* Return code */
nfsstat4 status = NFS4_OK;

switch (claim) {
case CLAIM_NULL:
    if ((data->minorversion > 0) &&
        !clientid->cid_cb.v41.cid_reclaim_complete)
        status = NFS4ERR_GRACE;
    break;

case CLAIM_FH: <------------------------
    if (data->minorversion == 0)
        status = NFS4ERR_NOTSUPP;
    break;

    rest conditions
}

if (status == NFS4_OK) {
    if (take_ref) {
        if (nfs_get_grace_status(want_grace)) {
            *grace_ref = true;
        } else {
            status = want_grace ? NFS4ERR_NO_GRACE
                                : NFS4ERR_GRACE; <-------------------
        }
    } else {
        *grace_ref = false;
    }
}
return status
'}]}, {'type': 'paragraph', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'The logs show:'}], 'attrs': {'localId': 'f498f13e0b5d'}}, {'type': 'codeBlock', 'attrs': {'localId': '0cd47a1f-48ab-453f-abd8-86e72a176a75'}, 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Jun 16 11:26:59: nfs4_op_open :NFS4 :DEBUG :open4_validate_claim failed
